    "answer": {
      "short": "Since $f(-x)=-f(x)$, $|f(-x)|=|-f(x)|=|f(x)|$. Hence $|f(x)|$ is even.",
      "worked": "Let $g(x)=|f(x)|$. Since $f$ is odd, $f(-x)=-f(x)$. Therefore\n$$\\begin{align*}g(-x)&=|f(-x)|\\\\g(-x)&=|-f(x)|\\\\g(-x)&=|f(x)|\\\\g(-x)&=g(x)\\end{align*}$$\nThus $g$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
